  "question": {
    "text": "$$\n\\text { A solid sphere of radius } R \\text { has moment of inertia } J \\text { about its qeometrical axis. If it is }\n$$\nmelted into a disc of radius $r$ and thickness $t$. If its moment of inertia about the tangential axis (which is perpendicular to plane of the disc), is also equal to $I$, then the value of $r$ is equal to\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/lSgwN8rcG18285o-EaZ9esu_dYPU3wCgkbldDfNUel8.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "FwD6d",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{15}} R$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "J8XyI",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} R$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CxvwE",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{15}} R$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BPe9m",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{15}} R$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{2}{3} M R^2=\\frac{1}{2} M r^2+M r^2$ or $\\frac{2}{3} M R^2=\\frac{3}{2} M r^2 \\Rightarrow r=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{15}} R$",
    "image": null
  },
